# Downloaded WHO DAK annexes. Third-party publications fetched rather than committed: each DAK
# publishes Web Annexes A-D as ~1 MB spreadsheets at stable URLs, and every domain has its own
# set. `dak_generator.py` names the URL and checksum per domain and prints the fetch command
# when a file is absent.
#
# Scoped to the annexes directory, NOT to `forms/who-dak/` — that path also holds the
# standard's code, and on a case-insensitive filesystem `forms/WHO-DAK/` and `forms/who-dak/`
# are the same directory, so a rule on the latter silently swallows the generator on Windows
# while tracking it on Linux.
forms/who-dak/*/annexes/
